  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned}<br />& \\mathrm{N}_2(\\mathrm{~g})+3 \\mathrm{H}_2(\\mathrm{~g}) \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{NH}_3 \\\\<br>& \\Delta \\mathrm{H}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{ve} \\\\<br>& \\Delta \\mathrm{~S}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{ve}<br />\\end{aligned}$<br />(As gaseous moles decreases).<br />(1) As temperature increases $\\frac{-\\Delta \\mathrm{H}_R^0}{T}$, decreases<br />(2) $\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^{\\circ}=-\\mathrm{RT} \\ln \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{eq}}$<br />$\\mathrm{R} \\ln \\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{eq}}=-\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{G}^0}{\\mathrm{~T}}$<br />(on increasing temperature in exothermic reaction $\\mathrm{K}_{\\text {eq }}$ decreases)<br />$\\Delta \\mathrm{H}^{\\circ}$ and $\\Delta \\mathrm{S}^{\\circ}$ are almost constant with temperature.",
